  "solution": {
    "text": "When a solution of a <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is treated with KI a red precipitate of <math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></math> is obtained which dissolves in excess KI to give a colourless solution <math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> . When the solution of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is treated with a solution of cobalt (II) thiocyanate a deep blue crystalline precipitate of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is formed. The reactions are as follows<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>–</mo></mrow></msup><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><math><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>–</mo></mrow></msup><mo>→</mo><munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>–</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow></munder></math><br /><math> <mrow>  <msup>   <mrow>    <mtext>Hg</mtext></mrow>   <mrow>    <mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow>  </msup>  <mo>+</mo><mtext>Co</mtext><msub>   <mrow>    <mo stretchy='false'>(</mo><mtext>SCN</mtext><mo stretchy='false'>)</mo></mrow>   <mn>2</mn>  </msub>  <mo>&#x2192;</mo><munder>   <mrow>    <mtext>Hg</mtext><msub>     <mrow>      <mo stretchy='false'>(</mo><mtext>SCN</mtext><mo stretchy='false'>)</mo></mrow>     <mn>2</mn>    </msub>    </mrow>   <mrow>    <mtext>Blue</mtext><mo>&#x00A0;</mo><mtext>crystal</mtext><mo>&#x00A0;</mo><mtext>line</mtext><mo>&#x00A0;</mo><mtext>ppt</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow>  </munder>  </mrow></math><br /><br />Here other ion <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> , <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> do not give precipitates formed in these reactions.",
